From 4783ee433139d4d3f5e370db08248c45c1762026 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nucleon Dev <dev@localhost>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 11:05:58 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(client): open allow-listed Nucleon confirmation links
 from MCP-UI cards

handleUIAction ignored `link` actions. It now handles them without ever
messaging the model: nucleonLinks.ts accepts only
http://127.0.0.1:8631 or :18631 with path "/" and hash #/actions/act_<16 hex>
(no credentials, query, whitespace or non-canonical spelling), and only while
the user's click is a live transient activation. The page opens in a new tab
with noopener,noreferrer; anything else is ignored. tool/intent/prompt
handling, the iframe sandbox and patches 0001/0002 are unchanged.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
